  "configuration_id": "config_022",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) is the clear strongest modality at 48.5% acc, while both image encoders are weak (resnet50: 20.8%, ViT-L: 22.7%). The central open question is whether the weak image signal adds complementary information in a multimodal setting or merely introduces noise that degrades the strong RNA performance. This experiment (config_022) tests that directly: it pairs the best-known RNA encoder (pca_n2000) with the better image encoder (ViT-L, which outperformed resnet50 in image-only), in the simplest multimodal setup (singleprofile, concat fusion) to avoid confounding from aggregation or complex fusion. If concat with ViT-L fails to beat the RNA-only baseline, it strongly suggests image adds little value and budget should shift to RNA improvements (multiprofile, better encoders). If it does help, it opens a productive exploitation path across fusion strategies and profile settings. Under a limited budget, resolving this architecture-level question is more informative than optimizing within a single modality."
}

